; ted-fileopen2-outmem-end (#1009, the fix when not even an empty text
; can be made): Open of a file whose first line is empty (a line item of
; 10 bytes, as the empty line of a new text); every AllocMem of 10 bytes
; (MEMF_PUBLIC) of TED's process after the three of the start fails, so
; after the first line the empty text outmem leaves fails too.  TED alone
; under inject (alerts answered; 4 such allocations fail in all on the
; sessions' system, the two of fileopen2 and outmem among them).
; Correct: the alert "Not enough memory for operation!", then TED ends
; with return code -1 (#357); the original redraws from the freed lines.
; @fixed #1009
; @file bo.bas "abc\n"
; @file other.bas "\nabc\n"
; @source F bo.bas
; @command TEDAB:tools/inject alerts allocfail=10-10/f=1+3 blitz2:ted @FILE@
; @expect stdout "inject: allocfail: 4 allocations failed"
; @expect stdout "inject: alert: Not enough memory for operation!"
; @expect stdout "inject: rc=-1"
timeout 20
wait screen
menu 0 1
wait freq "Name of file to load"
freq ok "TEDRUN:work/other.bas"
wait exit
